what did the poster and trailers reveal  about jordan peel's nope are aliens  truly involved there are still a lot of  questions to be answered so watch this  before you see nope last year on july  22nd 2021 jordan peele took to twitter  to release the new poster and title of  his upcoming film revealing that nope  would be released exactly one year from  the davis announcement now that release  date is fast approaching peel remained  tight-lipped about the movie for most of  the year including just a cloud emoji  with a poster revealed production took  place in june of 2021 and star kiki  palmer revealed that filming took place  in santa clarita california nope has  quite the cast to begin with the three  leads appear to be daniel kaluuya kiki  palmer and steven young kaluyo's  breakout role was none other than get  out for which his stunning performance  earned an oscar nomination for best  actor since then he's been appearing in  notable films left and right such as  black panther and judas and the black  messiah the latter of which earned him  his first oscar win meanwhile palmer  made waves for her supporting role in  2019's hustlers and also for her work in  the lead role in 2022's alice and  finally yen also received an oscar  nomination for his starring turn in  menari kaluya and palmer play siblings  oj and emerald haywood who own a ranch  in the first trailer emerald describes  him as the only black-owned horse  trainers in hollywood hen plays ricky  juke park who from the two released  trailers seems to be some sort of rodeo  announcer additionally the supporting  cast includes euphoria breakout barbie  ferreira the oa cast member brandon  perea and michael wincott from westworld  up until recently the plot of knope has  been kept under wraps even the first  trailer which was released in february  didn't tell us much besides the fact  that the ranch owners oj and emerald  began noticing alien-like objects in the  sky the eerie first trailer promises a  horror-filled movie going experience but  not much else specifically with the  second trailer we finally have a bit  more insight into the plot of nope it  seems as though oj and emerald began  experiencing weird potentially alien  related encounters after the mysterious  death of their father after o.j tells  emerald that he saw a very large object  above the clouds emerald asks if it  might have something to do with the  unexplained violence  you think whatever kill pops is out  there  then after witnessing the ominous  objects in the sky themselves the  siblings decide to try and capture the  moments on film to gain fame and fortune  once they provide proof of aliens they  even hire a tech-minded assistant angel  torres who works for fry's electronics  to help them out as well as a mysterious  man named antlers holst whom emerald  claims is the only person who is capable  of getting the strange invaders on film  even though the second trailer feels a  bit more lighthearted than the first we  can definitely expect horror to be at  the center of the story the first  official trailer for jordan peele's  upcoming film knope opens with edward  murray bridges the horse in motion  followed by emerald hayward's narration  about its significance as the first film  ever made she follows up by claiming  that she and her brother are related to  the writer and the short we then find  out that she is filming an advertisement  for her and her brother oj's hollywood  horse training services afterward we see  quick snippets of strange occurrences  happening around the small rural  california area where the horse training  stable resides this includes inflatable  wavy tube men deflating ominous shadows  enveloping everything and animals  freaking out it also seems to confirm  early rumors that the film will be about  aliens or at the very least otherworldly  creatures in some capacity midway  through the trailer there is what looks  like an alien hand outstretched towards  a human child's fist seemingly a direct  reference to e.t the extraterrestrial  right afterward there is a strange  looking creature scurrying in the  darkness obscured by shadows and fences  that appears to be chasing one of the  main characters as not to mention kaluya  riding on horseback is a shadow engulfs  the scenery like the saucers in  independence day and an abduction seeing  a palmer at the very end of the trailer  the second trailer further confirms the  alien invasion storyline with several  more shots of ufos flying through the  sky it even ends with oj bling on  horseback from a silver flying saucer  all jordan peel's titles are evocative  in one way or another get out was very  apt evoking racist messages along the  lines of get out of my neighborhood that  have been levied against black people in  the past meanwhile us refers to both the  connections between the characters and  their antagonistic doppelgangers as well  as us as an abbreviation for the united  states nope however might be the most  cryptic title so far some fans have  speculated that it might have to do with  the acronym n-o-p-e which would  supposedly stand for not of planet earth  it's above us writer director jordan  peele himself however has a different  interpretation stating in an interview  with entertainment weekly  this film is definitely a ride the title  speaks to the idea of being in tune with  what the audience is thinking and  feeling in the theater i know a lot of  people who say when it's a scary movie  they say nope especially black audiences  right we love horror but there's a  skepticism besides the posters and  trailers there's also a viral video for  nope that surfaced a while ago on jordan  peel's official twitter account it was  made to look like someone recording a  local news broadcast which reported on a  flood of yellow-headed blackbirds in  mexico falling out of the sky for some  mysterious reason since the film's  trailer shows horses getting spooked by  some unseen force it makes sense that  this force could be affecting other  animals like birds as well there is a  similar scene in m night shyamalan's  signs in which birds are killed in  mid-air by an unseen force in the case  of signs the birds crashed into cloaked  spaceships the reporter in the video  ends a broadcast by hypothesizing about  what the birds might be fleeing from  some experts say the blackbirds may have  been trying to escape a predatory bird  or perhaps they were attacked by a  spacecraft only time will tell for sure  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  no for coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

